      <p>Unlike graduation, which draws crowds to a single ceremony at a single time, move-in day spreads chaos across an entire morning as hundreds of families arrive within staggered but overlapping windows, each hauling a car's worth of belongings to a dorm that was not built with modern move-in volume in mind. Campus staff typically assign narrow drop-off windows by building or floor, and missing your window can mean circling the block, or the neighborhood, waiting for a new slot to open — a genuinely stressful way to start a student's college experience.</p>
